      "text": [
        " كَانَ عَلِيٌّ ( عليه السلام ) إِذَا وَجَدَ رَجُلَيْنِ فِي لِحَافٍ وَاحِدٍ مُجَرَّدَيْنِ جَلَدَهُمَا حَدَّ الزَّانِي مِائَةَ جَلْدَةٍ كُلَّ وَاحِدٍ مِنْهُمَا وَ كَذَا الْمَرْأَتَانِ إِذَا وُجِدَتَا فِي لِحَافٍ وَاحِدٍ مُجَرَّدَتَيْنِ جَلَدَ كُلَّ وَاحِدَةٍ مِنْهُمَا مِائَةَ جَلْدَةٍ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Mahboub, from Abu Ayoub, from Abu Ubeyda, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Ja’far<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘Ali<sup>asws</sup>, whenever he<sup>asws</sup> found two men in one quilt, naked, would whip both of them the Penalty (<span class=\"iTxt\">Hadd</span>) of the adultery, one hundred lashes, each one of them, and similarly for the two women if they were both found to be in one quilt, naked, would whip each one of them one hundred lashes’."
        ]
      }
